# Device-local HAL services. AOSP's vendor file_contexts labels the stock name
#   /(vendor|system/vendor)/bin/hw/android\.hardware\.audio@2\.0-service
# only; our audio HAL binary carries the ".m95" suffix (it binds /dev/binder
# instead of /dev/vndbinder, see audio_hal_service/service.cpp) so that anchored
# regex does not match it. Result observed live [DEV, 2026-08-09]:
#   ls -Z /vendor/bin/hw/android.hardware.audio@2.0-service.m95
#     -> u:object_r:vendor_file:s0
#   cat /proc/<pid of that service>/attr/current
#     -> u:r:init:s0
# i.e. no domain transition at all — the service runs in init's domain and every
# rule in sepolicy/hal_audio_default.te is dead code. It only "works" today
# because the device is Permissive (getenforce == Permissive).
/(system/)?vendor/bin/hw/android\.hardware\.audio@2\.0-service\.m95  u:object_r:hal_audio_default_exec:s0

# Fingerprint HAL. We ship the LineageOS @2.0-service (our blob is
# module_api_version 2.0; AOSP's @2.1-service rejects it), and the AOSP vendor
# file_contexts in this tree labels the @2.1 name ONLY. LineageOS does carry
# the @2.0 label — device/lineage/sepolicy/common/vendor/file_contexts:2 — but
# that directory is gated off for us: sepolicy.mk only adds it when
# TARGET_USES_PREBUILT_VENDOR_SEPOLICY != true, and this device satisfies both
# of its enabling conditions (TARGET_COPY_OUT_VENDOR is left at the default
# `vendor`, BoardConfig.mk:88, and BOARD_VENDORIMAGE_FILE_SYSTEM_TYPE is unset
# because there is no vendor partition), so it resolves to true and only
# common/dynamic is picked up. Without the line below the HAL would run in
# init's domain exactly like the audio service above.
# The optional (\.m95) covers our device-local fork of that service
# (device-18.1/meizu/m95/fingerprint): the module name had to differ from
# the upstream one it is built alongside, and a file_contexts pattern has
# to match the WHOLE path, so the plain @2.0-service line would miss it.
/(system/)?vendor/bin/hw/android\.hardware\.biometrics\.fingerprint@2\.0-service(\.m95)?  u:object_r:hal_fingerprint_default_exec:s0

