# fscreate before creating the node. Proof that this works on this device:
# /dev/socket/rild-debug, declared on the adjacent line (:138), comes up
# labelled rild_debug_socket, which can only come from plat file_contexts:152.
#
# FACT: without this line the node comes up u:object_r:socket_device:s0 (live
# `ls -laZ /dev/socket/rild-oem`, 2026-08-10) because plat_file_contexts labels
# only /dev/socket/rild and /dev/socket/rild-debug, and everything else in
# /dev/socket falls through to the socket_device default.
#
# The consumer is /vendor/bin/thermal (init.m95.thermal.rc:43, user/group
# system, which satisfies the 0660 radio:system DAC). It is the modem thermal
# control channel - `strings -a /vendor/bin/thermal` carries "rild-oem",
# "MDTM_TOG,%d", "set_md_toggle_throttle cur=%d set=%d", "setMdTpThreshold",
