# Same-process HALs.
#
# FACT (captures/a11-20260906/lastkmsg-v{6,7}.txt, three boots): zygote and
# mediaserver take `execute` denials on plain /vendor libraries --
#   avc: denied { execute } comm="main" path="/vendor/lib/libged.so"
#        scontext=u:r:zygote:s0 tcontext=u:object_r:vendor_file:s0
#   avc: denied { execute } ... path="/vendor/lib/libgralloc_extra.so" ...
# and public/domain.te:1328-1343 forbids every coredomain `vendor_file:file
# { execute open }` with no exemption for zygote. So under enforcing this
# cannot be granted: the libraries have to carry the type AOSP made for
# exactly this case.
#
# same_process_hal_file is that type: it is vendor_file_type (so it stays
# legal on /vendor), and private/zygote.te:173, private/system_server.te:268,
# private/webview_zygote.te:76, private/rs.te:27 and private/gpuservice.te:17
# already grant those five core domains { execute read open getattr map } on
# it. Vendor domains get it wholesale from public/domain.te:175-179.
#
# The set below is the passthrough graphics stack and its DT_NEEDED closure on
# /vendor, read off the built image with readelf, not guessed:
#   libGLES_mali.so    -> libm95shim_region, libged, libgpu_aux, libgralloc_extra
#   gralloc.mt6797.so  -> libm95shim_utils, libm95probe, libgralloc_extra, libion_mtk
#   libgralloc_extra   -> libged, libion_mtk
# Everything else in those closures (libbinder, libutils, libcutils, libhardware,
# libsync, libutilscallstack, libion, libGLESv1_CM) resolves from /system and is
# not on /vendor at all, so it needs no entry here.
#
# Deliberately NOT listed, because system/sepolicy/vendor/file_contexts:83-88
# already carries them: android.hardware.graphics.mapper@*-impl*.so,
# android.hardware.renderscript@1.0-impl.so, gralloc.default.so, libhwbinder.so,
# libhidltransport.so. The gralloc line below is still needed -- AOSP names only
# gralloc.default.so, and our real module is gralloc.mt6797.so.
/(vendor|system/vendor)/lib(64)?/hw/gralloc\..*\.so     u:object_r:same_process_hal_file:s0
/(vendor|system/vendor)/lib(64)?/libged\.so             u:object_r:same_process_hal_file:s0
/(vendor|system/vendor)/lib(64)?/libgpu_aux\.so         u:object_r:same_process_hal_file:s0
/(vendor|system/vendor)/lib(64)?/libgralloc_extra\.so   u:object_r:same_process_hal_file:s0
/(vendor|system/vendor)/lib(64)?/libion_mtk\.so         u:object_r:same_process_hal_file:s0
/(vendor|system/vendor)/lib(64)?/libm95shim_region\.so  u:object_r:same_process_hal_file:s0
/(vendor|system/vendor)/lib(64)?/libm95shim_utils\.so   u:object_r:same_process_hal_file:s0
/(vendor|system/vendor)/lib(64)?/libm95probe\.so        u:object_r:same_process_hal_file:s0

# 2026-09-24 (Android 13, SELinux lane): the closure above was one link short.
# libgpu_aux.so now pulls libdpframework.so, and through it the MDP/PQ/codec
# helpers below. FACT (capture m95-boot-20260924-192234, dmesg): zygote,
# surfaceflinger and bootanim take { execute } / { open read getattr } on
# vendor_file for /vendor/lib{,64}/libdpframework.so, libbwc.so, libm4u.so,
# libpq_prot.so and /vendor/lib/libstdc++.so. The kernel audits a
# (domain, vendor_file, file, perm) tuple once per boot, so the log names only
# the first library per permission; the full set is the readelf DT_NEEDED
# closure of egl/libGLES_mali.so + hw/gralloc.mt6797.so on the built /vendor
# (64- and 32-bit). Under enforcing any one of them missing means no EGL in
# zygote, surfaceflinger or bootanim.
/(vendor|system/vendor)/lib(64)?/libdpframework\.so      u:object_r:same_process_hal_file:s0
/(vendor|system/vendor)/lib(64)?/libbwc\.so              u:object_r:same_process_hal_file:s0
/(vendor|system/vendor)/lib(64)?/libm4u\.so              u:object_r:same_process_hal_file:s0
/(vendor|system/vendor)/lib(64)?/libmtk_drvb\.so         u:object_r:same_process_hal_file:s0
/(vendor|system/vendor)/lib(64)?/libpq_prot\.so          u:object_r:same_process_hal_file:s0
/(vendor|system/vendor)/lib(64)?/libpqservice\.so        u:object_r:same_process_hal_file:s0
/(vendor|system/vendor)/lib(64)?/libvcodec_utility\.so   u:object_r:same_process_hal_file:s0
/(vendor|system/vendor)/lib(64)?/libvcodecdrv\.so        u:object_r:same_process_hal_file:s0
/(vendor|system/vendor)/lib(64)?/libvcodec_oal\.so       u:object_r:same_process_hal_file:s0
/(vendor|system/vendor)/lib(64)?/libmp4enc_sa\.ca7\.so   u:object_r:same_process_hal_file:s0
/(vendor|system/vendor)/lib(64)?/libvc1dec_sa\.ca7\.so   u:object_r:same_process_hal_file:s0
/(vendor|system/vendor)/lib(64)?/libvp8dec_sa\.ca7\.so   u:object_r:same_process_hal_file:s0
/(vendor|system/vendor)/lib(64)?/libstdc\+\+\.so          u:object_r:same_process_hal_file:s0
/(vendor|system/vendor)/lib(64)?/libnetutils\.so         u:object_r:same_process_hal_file:s0

# A13 GSI (FACT 2026-09-11): the AOSP regex covers only ...-service, not the
# .software variant this device installs; unlabeled -> init refuses to start it
# -> LockSettingsService NPE on IGateKeeper.
/(vendor|system/vendor)/bin/hw/android\.hardware\.gatekeeper@1\.0-service\.software  u:object_r:hal_gatekeeper_default_exec:s0

