# 2026-09-24 (Android 13, SELinux lane).

# HIDL clearkey. A13's system/sepolicy/vendor/file_contexts:36 labels only the
# AIDL android.hardware.drm-service.clearkey; the @1.4 HIDL binary this build
# still installs stayed vendor_file, so init ran it in its own domain. FACT
# (both captures): "File /vendor/bin/hw/android.hardware.drm@1.4-service.
# clearkey (labeled "u:object_r:vendor_file:s0") has incorrect label or no
# domain transition" x26, and init itself adding IDrmFactory to
# hwservicemanager. Under enforcing init refuses to start it
# (system/core/init/service.cpp:97). hal_drm_default is the A13 domain for
# HIDL DRM factories and already serves hal_drm_hwservice.
/(vendor|system/vendor)/bin/hw/android\.hardware\.drm@1\.4-service\.clearkey  u:object_r:hal_drm_default_exec:s0

# zram. The plat label is ram_device (private/file_contexts:87), which A13
# gives neither init (swapon) nor toolbox (mkswap); swap_block_device is the
# type both hold rights on. FACT (both captures): denied { write } zram0
# scontext=init and { read write open ioctl getattr } comm=mkswap
# scontext=toolbox, tcontext=ram_device. Under enforcing: no zram swap.
/dev/block/zram0        u:object_r:swap_block_device:s0

# Modem config store (file.te ccci_cfg_file).
/data/ccci_cfg(/.*)?    u:object_r:ccci_cfg_file:s0
